# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# CAMP-1: the Encamp Fix's report leaves with the camp screen (M5-E1e,
# #298) — camp entry, the Fix, and the menu's own EXIT, with nothing of
# the seam's left on the adventuring screen afterwards.
#
# **Why this leg exists.** The report's title used to be handed to the
# program's frame, which draws it on the box's own top row, 0x11 — and
# the camp loop's own way out clears rows 0x12..0x16 of the panel and
# the message line on 0x18, nothing above them. So `FIX: PARTY HEALED`
# stayed on the screen under the adventuring bar after camp was gone,
# seen by a person on a display. The title is a line on 0x12 now, and the
# `allow` after the exit below is the assertion: from the frame after
# the mode word leaves camp to the end of the run, the seam-on screen is
# the seam-off screen everywhere but two named cells.
#
# **A pair leg, and it can be one.** Every key here reaches the program
# in both halves: `E` is ENCAMP on the adventuring bar, `F` on the camp
# bar is the Fix with the seam on and a letter the camp loop compares
# against its own commands and ignores with it off, and `E` on the camp
# bar is EXIT either way. Slot C's party is whole, so the Fix declines and
# the report is `FIX: PARTY HEALED` over `NO HIT POINTS RESTORED.` — the
# case the screenshot showed, and one with no cast, no rest and no clock
# in it to move the two runs apart.
#
# **Driven, on the shorter boot.** This script is the boot #291 left —
# the code-wheel seam on and told the challenge is answered — so there is
# no wheel letter and no Return in it, and its frames are not the older
# legs' frames. The runner does not yet carry that flag (#293 owes every
# leg its re-drive on the new boot), so this leg was driven by hand with
# the same host, the same disk copy, the same dump cadence and the same
# check the runner makes: 463 frames compared, 1 of them a dump apart,
# every difference inside the rects below. Before the change, the same
# script leaves row 0x11 holding the title's 394 pixels from frame 10,250
# to the end of the run, and rows 0x12..0x16 holding nothing.
about the Encamp Fix's report leaves with the camp screen: camp, FIX, EXIT
kind pair
program START.EXE
both code-wheel
seam encamp-fix
until 230000000
every 25
# A screen may appear in the two runs a dump apart, because a repaint
# lands where it lands — here the camp teardown itself, 8 frames apart in
# the two runs. One dump of slack, the same as every other leg.
slack 1

# Slot C: four strong, whole, and standing where it can camp. ENCAMP once
# the adventuring screen has settled; the Fix once the camp bar is up
# (the camp screen's own redraw is slow — it reads the banner off the
# disk — and a press that lands during it is drained); EXIT once the
# report has been on the screen a while.
key L@7550
key C@7800
key E@8800
key F@9600
key E@10200

# What the seam owns. The bar is the camp screen's own command bar with
# `FIX` spliced into it and the prompt blanked for the one call. The
# panel is rows 0x12..0x16 of the message panel — the box's rows since
# #298, and deliberately not 0x11: the frame is handed no title, so that
# row is blank in both runs and this rect says so by leaving it out.
rect bar 0,192,319,199
rect panel 8,144,311,183
# Two cells that are not the seam's drawing and are named rather than
# hidden. The knot is the corner tile of the viewport box at column 0x10
# of row 0x10, which the report's frame paints over with a plain edge
# tile — as the program's own cast screen from camp does, and nothing on
# the EXIT path repaints. The banner is the 3D inset, where the camp
# picture's fire animates on the program's clock: the seam's batches
# shift the program by a few frames and the two runs' flames fall out of
# phase by more than one dump, so it is masked, and this leg says nothing
# about it.
rect knot 128,128,135,135
rect banner 24,24,111,111

# Up to the camp bar: not one pixel. The mode word becomes camp at frame
# 8,991 and the camp screen's bar is up by 9,450.
allow 0-9425 none
# The spliced bar, before the Fix is chosen.
allow 9450-9625 bar banner
# The report, on the pass after the command declined, until the exit.
allow 9650-10225 bar panel knot banner
# Out of camp. The mode word leaves camp at 10,227 (10,219 with the seam
# off) and nothing of the box is on the screen after it. The bar is the
# adventuring bar in both runs, with its highlight on a different
# command: the highlight is one byte in the data segment every bar reads
# and clamps to its own group count, and the spliced bar has one group
# more, so the same EXIT leaves it on a different number.
allow 10250-end knot bar
